\description{
One row per household in the waste characterisation study of the Gulu City
household solid waste study. Each household stored the waste it generated
over seven consecutive days in bags provided by the study team; the bags
were weighed on 1 to 3 October 2026 and the waste was sorted by hand into
16 fractions adapted from ASTM D5231. The table holds the total weights,
the per capita generation rate, the bulk density measured with a 10 litre
bucket and the weight of every fraction before and after the deduction of
the container weight, for 95 households of which 94 are included in the
averages of the study. The waste records cannot be linked to the
households of guluswm_survey.
}
